--- !u!114 &1477808482
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1477808481}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5b555b02773f820439e56f06b05e26eb, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  sonar: {fileID: 211081082}
  terminalText: {fileID: 868041953}
  display: {fileID: 454797055}
  Numpad: {fileID: 1535851451}
  clickPressed: {fileID: 1535851453}
  clickReleased: {fileID: 1535851452}
  TerminalCanvas: {fileID: 1751144876}
  radioMessages:
  - "\"Hello? Hello hello? You there, Newbie? Okay, if you can hear me, that means
    you were able to figure out the Radio. Good news, good news. If you can\u2019t
    hear me, too bad. I don\u2019t really got all day to wait around and watch ya
    press buttons till you find the right frequency, yanno? Let\u2019s see here\u2026
    Huh, that\u2019s new. Gettin\u2019 some funky echo through the speaker\u2026
    must be \u2018cause it\u2019s old. Yeah, yeah\u2026 This is way too much too
    fast for a newbie like you. How \u2018bout this for now: I\u2019m Keith, The
    Halley Company\u2019s resident Radio Guy. I\u2019ll be broadcasting every once
    in a while to help ya out in your diving bell, so don\u2019t forget this frequency,
    you hear? Okay, what else\u2026 Oh, right, right. Just so you know, I can\u2019t
    actually see inside the Bell. So you\u2019ve got some privacy, just\u2026 don\u2019t
    do anything weird, \u2018kay? You don\u2019t wanna go down as that guy. Anyways,
    should be a panel of Switches somewhere. Flip \u2018em all on, and the Bell\u2019ll
    start to descend. I\u2019ll let you go, then\u2014 it\u2019s gonna take a sec
    to get your bearings once things start movin\u2019, trust me. Talk to you soon-ish.
    And congrats on becoming Operator.\""
  - "\"Hello? Ya there, Op? Hope you don\u2019t mind a good ol\u2019 nickname. Me
    again. Forgot to mention somethin\u2019 kinda important. Whoops. The Bell might
    look a bit different from what you saw during the briefing\u2014 this is an older
    model from a few years back. It doesn\u2019t have all those fancy features that
    the new ones do, so you\u2019re gonna hafta maintain this guy for your entire
    expedition. And, whilst that is a little bit unfortunate, I personally think
    it gives ya somethin\u2019 to do while you\u2019re plungin\u2019 into the \u201Cdeep
    wonders of below,\u201D as The Halley Company likes to say, you know? But yeah.
    Simple, standard stuff. There should be a Gauge somewhere\u2014 hear any steam
    releasing? Well, if so, that\u2019s no good, no good at all. Give the lever attached
    to the pipe a press, \u2018n that\u2019ll gradually normalize the pressure in
    there. You\u2019ll know it worked if the red light turns off. Got it got it?
    It was a huge pain in the ass to get the last Bell up when the Operator didn\u2019t
    maintain it, so let\u2019s just stay on top of that for everyone\u2019s sake,
    okay? Good luck, buddy. Catch ya later.\""
  - "\"Hello? Yoohoo, Newbie. Just Keith, checkin\u2019 in. Aren\u2019t I nice? So\u2026
    anything new or unusual on your end? Strange, strange voices in your head? Funky
    colours on the walls? Well, if I\u2019m gonna be honest here, we\u2019re detecting
    some anomalous behaviour. Can you flick up all\u2014 I\u2019ve got, umm, documentation
    here, you see. Says somethin\u2019 about checking the switchbox under troubleshooting\u2026
    That\u2014 the red light, I mean\u2014 shouldn\u2019t be happening. Who knows
    what\u2019s goin\u2019 on? I sure don\u2019t. But I\u2014 I do know that red
    lights are usually a warning to maintain the Bell\u2019s systems. You should
    probably deal with that. And keep an eye on it, would ya? The Bell you\u2019re
    in is an older model, so it might keep happenin\u2019. Have you tried flicking
    them off and back on again? Ta-ta for now.\""
